  "solution": "[IMAGE: https://cdn.repeatermock.com/tb/e306d0edaa1c360a9dc63af39b3f34da9440d14853e714d54d6553647fbc3ba8.png] \n\nGiven equation: 25 - 28 + 21 × 10 ÷ 5 = 43\n\nOption 1) 5 and 28\n\nAfter interchanging the numbers we get:\n\n⇒ 25 - 5 + **__21 × 10 ÷ 28__** = 43\n\n⇒ __**25**__ - 5 __**+ 7.5**__ = 43\n\n⇒ __32.5____ -** 5**__ = 43\n\n⇒ 27.5 = 43\n\nOption 2) **21 and 25**\n\nAfter interchanging the numbers we get:\n\n⇒ 21 - 28 + __**25 × 1**0 ÷ 5__ = 43\n\n⇒ __**21**__ - 28 __**+ 50**__ = 43\n\n⇒ __**71 - 28**__ = 43\n\n**⇒ 43 = 43**\n\nOption 3) 10 and 43\n\nAfter interchanging the signs we get:\n\n⇒ 25 - 28 + __**21 × 43 ÷ 5**__ = 10\n\n⇒ __**25**__ - 28 + __180.6__ = 10\n\n⇒ __205.6** - 28**__ = 10\n\n⇒ 177.6 = 10\n\nOption 4) 21 and 28\n\nAfter interchanging the signs we get:\n\n⇒ 25 - 21 + __**28 × 10 ÷ 5**__ = 43\n\n⇒ __**25**__ - 21 + __56__ = 43\n\n⇒ __81** - 21**__ = 43\n\n⇒ 60 = 43\n\nHence, the correct answer is \"21 and 25\".",
